%% Figure 12 — Business Catalog Governance
flowchart LR
  Admin([Active PM with UserAdmin]) --> UI[Business Catalogs workspace\nModules, Components, Defect Categories and valid pairs]
  UI --> Auth{CAP confirms exactly one PM role\nand UserAdmin capability?}
  Auth -- No --> Denied[403 denied\nNo catalog disclosure or mutation]
  Auth -- Yes --> Operation{Requested operation}
  Operation -- Read/search --> Read[CAP returns authorized\nfiltered catalog rows]
  Operation -- Create or edit --> Write[Normalize allowlisted fields\nand preserve immutable ID]
  Operation -- Activate --> Activate[Validate ETag and active parents]
  Operation -- Deactivate --> Impact[Read Bug, responsibility\nand active-child impact counts]
  Operation -- Delete --> Delete[405 DELETE forbidden\nHistorical references preserved]

  Write --> Guard{Valid code/name or pair, unique,\ncurrent ETag and active parents?}
  Activate --> Guard
  Impact --> Reason{Reason supplied and no active\nresponsibility or child dependency?}
  Guard -- No --> Reject[400/404/409 safe response\nNo catalog mutation]
  Reason -- No --> Reject
  Guard -- Yes --> Persist[(Create or update catalog item)]
  Reason -- Yes --> Deactivate[(Set active = false\nDo not rewrite historical Bugs)]

  Persist --> Audit[Append allowlisted success audit\nwith safe before/after values]
  Deactivate --> Audit
  Reject --> RejectionAudit[Append sanitized rejection audit\nwhen a target is known]
  Audit --> Reload[Reload catalog list and active value helps]
  RejectionAudit --> Reload
  Read --> Display([Display governed catalog state])
  Reload --> Display
  Delete --> Display

